# 必考词 Unit09
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit09核心高频词汇

{{enthusiasm}}{/ɪnˈθjuːziæzəm/}}{n. 热情；热忱}}{{She showed great enthusiasm for the new project.}}

{{entire}}{/ɪnˈtaɪər/}}{adj. 整个的；全部的}}{{The entire team worked overtime to meet the deadline.}}

{{entity}}{/ˈentəti/}}{n. 实体；存在}}{{The company operates as a separate legal entity.}}

{{environment}}{/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/}}{n. 环境}}{{Protecting the environment is everyone's responsibility.}}

{{episode}}{/ˈepɪsəʊd/}}{n. 一段经历；插曲}}{{The most exciting episode of the series aired last night.}}

{{equality}}{/ɪˈkwɒləti/}}{n. 平等；相等}}{{The organization fights for gender equality in the workplace.}}

{{equip}}{/ɪˈkwɪp/}}{v. 装备；配备}}{{The lab is equipped with the latest technology.}}

{{equivalent}}{/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/}}{adj. 等价的；n. 等价物}}{{One mile is roughly equivalent to 1.6 kilometers.}}

{{era}}{/ˈɪərə/}}{n. 时代；纪元}}{{We are living in the era of digital transformation.}}

{{erode}}{/ɪˈrəʊd/}}{v. 侵蚀；腐蚀}}{{Wind and rain erode the surface of rocks over time.}}

{{error}}{/ˈerər/}}{n. 错误；过失}}{{The report contained several factual errors.}}

{{escape}}{/ɪˈskeɪp/}}{v./n. 逃跑；逃避}}{{The prisoners attempted to escape from the jail.}}

{{essential}}{/ɪˈsenʃl/}}{adj. 必要的；本质的}}{{Water is essential for the survival of all living things.}}

{{establish}}{/ɪˈstæblɪʃ/}}{v. 建立；确立}}{{The university was established in 1920.}}

{{estimate}}{/ˈestɪmeɪt/}}{v./n. 估计；评价}}{{The cost of the project is estimated at $5 million.}}

{{evaluate}}{/ɪˈvæljueɪt/}}{v. 评估；评价}}{{The committee will evaluate all the applications carefully.}}

{{evidence}}{/ˈevɪdəns/}}{n. 证据；迹象}}{{There is strong evidence to support the theory.}}

{{evil}}{/ˈiːvl/}}{adj. 邪恶的；n. 邪恶}}{{The character in the novel represents pure evil.}}

{{evolve}}{/ɪˈvɒlv/}}{v. 进化；发展}}{{Technology has evolved rapidly over the past few decades.}}

{{exaggerate}}{/ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt/}}{v. 夸张；夸大}}{{He tends to exaggerate his achievements.}}

{{exceed}}{/ɪkˈsiːd/}}{v. 超过；超出}}{{The results exceeded our expectations.}}

{{exception}}{/ɪkˈsepʃn/}}{n. 例外}}{{Without exception, all students must take the final exam.}}

{{excess}}{/ɪkˈses/}}{n. 过量；adj. 过量的}}{{An excess of sugar in the diet can lead to health problems.}}

{{exchange}}{/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/}}{v./n. 交换；交流}}{{The students participated in a cultural exchange program.}}

{{exclude}}{/ɪkˈskluːd/}}{v. 排除；排斥}}{{The price excludes tax and delivery charges.}}

{{exclusive}}{/ɪkˈskluːsɪv/}}{adj. 独有的；排他的}}{{The hotel offers exclusive services to VIP guests.}}

{{execute}}{/ˈeksɪkjuːt/}}{v. 执行；处决}}{{The plan was executed flawlessly by the team.}}

{{exert}}{/ɪɡˈzɜːrt/}}{v. 施加；运用}}{{Parents exert a great influence on their children's behavior.}}

{{exhaust}}{/ɪɡˈzɔːst/}}{v. 使精疲力竭；用尽}}{{The long hike exhausted everyone in the group.}}

{{exhibit}}{/ɪɡˈzɪbɪt/}}{v. 展示；表现；n. 展品}}{{The artist exhibited her paintings at the gallery.}}

{{expand}}{/ɪkˈspænd/}}{v. 扩大；膨胀}}{{The company plans to expand its operations to Asia.}}

{{expedition}}{/ˌekspɪˈdɪʃn/}}{n. 远征；探险}}{{The expedition to the South Pole lasted three months.}}

{{expense}}{/ɪkˈspens/}}{n. 费用；开支}}{{Travel expenses will be covered by the company.}}

{{experiment}}{/ɪkˈsperɪmənt/}}{n./v. 实验；试验}}{{The experiment proved the hypothesis to be correct.}}

{{explicit}}{/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/}}{adj. 明确的；直言的}}{{The instructions must be explicit and easy to follow.}}

{{exploit}}{/ɪkˈsplɔɪt/}}{v. 开发；剥削}}{{The company was accused of exploiting its workers.}}

{{explore}}{/ɪkˈsplɔːr/}}{v. 探索；考察}}{{Scientists continue to explore the mysteries of the universe.}}

{{explosion}}{/ɪkˈspləʊʒn/}}{n. 爆炸；激增}}{{The population explosion has put pressure on resources.}}

{{expose}}{/ɪkˈspəʊz/}}{v. 暴露；揭露}}{{The investigation exposed widespread corruption in the government.}}

{{extend}}{/ɪkˈstend/}}{v. 延伸；扩展}}{{The deadline has been extended by one week.}}
